issues.body:
We have logic to generate interactions.

But, game-players are wary that an interaction may fall between the cracks - so they want to be able to generate one manually.

So, we need to add a new popup form to `AdjudicationMessagesList`.  The popup form will let the adjudicator provide some data.

The layout of the form is provided here: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/185IQEG_yy3_16B3nDjqKWsGaigb2I54_IhqeVa0T-RY/edit#slide=id.g1d4daf1b3ae_0_0

This will be a collaborative piece of work:
- Ian can handle collating the data [1]
- Ian can provide the `Submit` handler [2]
- @lebaphi will create the form, please.  I _guess_ this will be something like the existing `CustomDialog`, but in the `helpers` sub-folder of `adjudication-messages-list`.

I don't really know how we do the form, or get the data in/out - so could to with @lebaphi  support on it.  Aah, hold on - I have a better understanding now.  The component will take these props:
```
export type Props = {
   // data to use to populate controls
   data: ManualInteractionData
   // close handler
   onClose: { (): void }
   // save handler, provides data from form controls
   onSave: { (data: ManualInteractionResults): void }
}
```

Note: I've started my bits, in #2251 

[1] See the `manualDialog` object
[2] See the `handleManualInteraction` method
